pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The `Cardinality` copy: all coefficients are one and the degree fits `i64`, so
% `1 x1 1 x2 >= i64::MIN` is stored as a cardinality constraint, whose `substitute` lowered the
% degree with an unchecked `-= 1` per literal mapped to TRUE. Same wrap, same forged UNSAT.
f 2;
rup 1 x1 1 x2 >= -9223372036854775808 ;
red 1 ~x1 >= 1 : x1 -> 1 ;
pol 1 4 +;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 5;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
